"""The storage of the files of the file fields (ADR 0027).

{% if st.s3 %}
The app keeps the files in the bucket of an S3-compatible service
(`{{ st.variables["bucket_env"] }}`). Without a bucket, for example on the machine of a
developer and in the tests, it keeps them in the folder of
`{{ st.variables["folder_env"] }}`. A record keeps each file as a JSON value (`StoredFile`): the
{% else %}
The app keeps the files in the folder of `{{ st.variables["folder_env"] }}`. A record keeps
each file as a JSON value (`StoredFile`): the
{% endif %}
key of the file in the storage, the name, the size, and the media type.
The key is new for each upload, so that a cache never shows an old file.

The read schemas give a signed link to each file (`/file-links/<token>`),
which ends after `STORAGE_LINK_SECONDS`, so that an `<img src>` works
without a sign-in. The app gives a link only with a read of its record,
so the access rules of the read apply.
"""

